# netsurf: CSS stroke on inline SVG; presentation attributes settle against CSS (patch 358, with 358-libcss)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 357, with 358-libcss)
#
#  - css/hints.c: the stroke and stroke-width presentation attributes
#    become zero-specificity hints, as fill already was, so author CSS
#    outranks them in the cascade (a class with stroke: none beats
#    stroke="#00f").
#  - vb_inline_svg.c: stroke and stroke-width join 357's per-element
#    cascade. Where an element has the attribute (fill, stroke or
#    stroke-width), the computed value -- attribute and CSS already settled
#    -- is written in its place. Without one, a value differing from the
#    parent's is written. The rest inherits. On the root a CSS stroke other
#    than none, or a width other than 1, fills a missing attribute.
#    stroke-width is written in user units: a CSS px inside an SVG is a
#    user unit, scaled by the viewBox. It is printed with integers only
#    (the Vita's newlib may lack float printf).
#
# Changing the libcss headers needs a clean netsurf build (build/Linux-vita
# and build/Linux-vita-sim moved aside).
#
# Gate: CSS-svg-stroke (file:// snapshot, five pixels exact as Chromium:
# class stroke + width; root stroke: currentColor; CSS width beats the
# attribute; CSS stroke: none beats the attribute). CSS-svg-child-css and
# CSS-svg-fill-inherit are unchanged. Full fresh scorecard (r78-358 vs
# r77): mean 85.1 -> 85.2. wpnews' white stroked search icon now draws.
# Other diffs are live content.
